======================================================================
2.1 WHAT IS SYNTAX?
======================================================================

Syntax means the set of rules that define how a program
must be written in a programming language.

Think about human language:

    Correct:
        "I am learning C."

    Incorrect:
        "Learning C am I."

Programming languages also have rules.

Example of valid C:

    int age = 25;

Example of invalid C:

    int = age 25;


The compiler checks whether your source code follows
the rules of the C language.


IMPORTANT:

    Syntax = Structure/form of the code

    Semantics = Meaning/behavior of the code


Example:

    int x = 10;

This is syntactically valid and has a meaningful operation:
    Declare an integer variable x and initialize it to 10.


======================================================================
2.2 BASIC C PROGRAM
======================================================================

Example:

    #include <stdio.h>

    int main(void)
    {
        printf("Hello World\n");

        return 0;
    }


Breakdown:

    #include <stdio.h>
        → Preprocessor directive

    int
        → Return type

    main
        → Function name

    (void)
        → No parameters

    {
        ...
    }
        → Function body

    printf(...)
        → Function call

    ;
        → Statement terminator

    return 0;
        → Return statement


======================================================================
2.3 C TOKENS
======================================================================

A TOKEN is one of the smallest meaningful lexical elements
recognized by the C language.

Major categories include:

    1. Keywords
    2. Identifiers
    3. Constants
    4. String literals
    5. Operators
    6. Punctuators


Example:

    int age = 25;


Tokens:

    int
    age
    =
    25
    ;


Another example:

    sum = a + b;


Tokens:

    sum
    =
    a
    +
    b
    ;


Understanding tokens is important because the compiler
first performs lexical analysis of the source code.


======================================================================
2.4 LEXICAL ANALYSIS — BASIC IDEA
======================================================================

When a C program is compiled, one of the early stages
is lexical analysis.

Conceptually:

    Source code
         ↓
    Characters
         ↓
    Lexical analysis
         ↓
    Tokens
         ↓
    Parsing / syntax analysis
         ↓
    Further compilation


Example:

    int sum = a + b;


Lexical analysis recognizes approximately:

    KEYWORD       → int
    IDENTIFIER    → sum
    OPERATOR      → =
    IDENTIFIER    → a
    OPERATOR      → +
    IDENTIFIER    → b
    PUNCTUATOR    → ;


You do not manually perform lexical analysis;
the compiler does it.


