======================================================================
2.41 COMMON SYNTAX ERRORS
======================================================================

ERROR 1:

    Missing semicolon

    int x = 10


Correct:

    int x = 10;


ERROR 2:

    Missing closing brace

    int main(void)
    {
        printf("Hello");


Correct:

    int main(void)
    {
        printf("Hello");
        return 0;
    }


ERROR 3:

    Invalid identifier

    int 1age;


Correct:

    int age1;


ERROR 4:

    Using a keyword as identifier

    int int = 10;


Invalid.


ERROR 5:

    Wrong quote type

    char grade = "A";


This is not a correct way to initialize a single char.


Correct:

    char grade = 'A';


ERROR 6:

    String using single quotes

    printf('Hello');


Correct:

    printf("Hello");


