2.54 INTERVIEW QUESTIONS
======================================================================

Q1. What is syntax?

    Syntax is the set of rules that determine the valid
    structure of C source code.


Q2. What is a token?

    A token is a basic lexical element recognized by
    the compiler during lexical analysis.


Q3. What are the major categories of C tokens?

    Common categories:

        • Keywords
        • Identifiers
        • Constants
        • String literals
        • Operators
        • Punctuators


Q4. What is an identifier?

    A name used to identify a program entity.


Q5. Is C case-sensitive?

    Yes.


Q6. Can an identifier start with a number?

    No.


Q7. Can a keyword be used as a variable name?

    No.


Q8. Difference between 'A' and "A"?

    'A' is a character constant.

    "A" is a string literal containing A followed
    by a terminating null character.


Q9. What is a statement?

    A statement is an executable/declarative construct
    forming part of a C program.


Q10. What is a block?

    A sequence of declarations/statements enclosed
    in braces.


Q11. What is an expression?

    A combination of operands, operators, function calls,
    constants, etc., that represents a computation/value.


Q12. What is initialization?

    Giving an object its initial value when it is defined.


Q13. What is assignment?

    Storing a new value into an already existing
    modifiable object.


Q14. What is a header file?

    A file containing declarations, macros, types,
    and related interfaces intended to be shared
    among source files.


Q15. What is the purpose of #include?

    It is a preprocessing directive used to include
    the contents of a header file into the translation unit.


