2.57 CHAPTER 2 — MOST IMPORTANT POINTS
======================================================================

Remember these:

    1. Syntax defines the valid structure of C programs.

    2. C is case-sensitive.

    3. Tokens are the basic lexical elements of C.

    4. Important token categories include:
           Keywords
           Identifiers
           Constants
           String literals
           Operators
           Punctuators

    5. Keywords are reserved words.

    6. Identifiers are names given to program entities.

    7. Identifiers cannot start with a digit.

    8. Spaces are not allowed inside identifiers.

    9. 'A' is a character constant.

   10. "A" is a string literal.

   11. Semicolon usually terminates a statement.

   12. Braces define blocks.

   13. Expressions represent computations/values.

   14. Initialization gives an object its initial value.

   15. Assignment changes the value of an existing
       modifiable object.

   16. Comments are used to explain code.

   17. #include is a preprocessing directive.

   18. C does not use indentation to define blocks;
       braces do that.

   19. Readable formatting is still essential for
       professional programming.

   20. Compiler warnings should be taken seriously.


